    {
      "requirement_id": "req_576b89e9277ca12ad0f5",
      "requirement_type": "OUTPUT_PATH",
      "criticality": "HARD",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/lake-warming-attribution/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 7,
        "line_end": 7,
        "exact_text": "First, I want to do a trend analysis to determine whether there is a long-term warming trend for the water temperature. You should output the 'trend_result.csv' in '/root/output/'. The file should have two columns: one is \"slope,\" and the other is \"p-value.\"\n",
        "source_sha256": "5c9d251ad77db347e6260049060c18e80f0c5c42b89029e136a70b245d7c90e0",
        "extraction_rule": "actionable_paragraph"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_84db63232a2fdcbe7dfc",
      "requirement_type": "OUTPUT_PATH",
      "criticality": "HARD",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/lake-warming-attribution/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 9,
        "line_end": 9,
        "exact_text": "Second, I want to know the most important driving factor behind the water warming. To simplify, all driving factors listed in our data can be classified into Heat, Flow, Wind, and Human. Then, you can just tell me which category is the most important category, and what percentage of this category contributes to the water warming. You should output the 'dominant_factor.csv' in '/root/output/'. The file should have two columns: one is \"variable,\" and the other is \"contribution.\" You only need to output the most important variable.\n",
        "source_sha256": "5c9d251ad77db347e6260049060c18e80f0c5c42b89029e136a70b245d7c90e0",
        "extraction_rule": "actionable_paragraph"
      }
    }
  ],
